<title>GERMANY: RWE's petrol unit DEA buys KEH from Kloeckner.</title>
<headline>RWE's petrol unit DEA buys KEH from Kloeckner.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>German oil company DEA Mineraloel AG, the petroleum and chemical unit of diversified energy group RWE AG, said on Thursday it had bought Kloeckner Energiehandel AG (KEH) from Kloeckner &amp; Co.</p>
<p>KEH is Kloeckner's main energy unit and Kloeckner said that the sale would leave it free to concentrate on its international distribution activities. Kloeckner &amp; Co is a unit of RWE's rival energy group Viag AG.</p>
<p>KEH had 380 employees in 1995, when it reported turnover of 1.1 billion marks.</p>
<p>DEA said that the acquisition is subject to the approval of German cartel authorities as well as the Kloeckner board.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
